#   LAN to Internet - internet.https: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   LAN to Internet - standard.dns: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   LAN to Internet - standard.ping: the source of the rule is in zone eth1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind eth1 with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone WAN, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   Internet to Webserver - internet.https: the source of the rule is in zone WAN, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone eth2, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind eth2 with --zone-network
